Every change of what VNAS is doing stops the pet's motion in dsh-pet, its own walk and the move
to a position it was told to go to alike. A turn that moves the pet ends right after the command,
so the pet stopped halfway, or before it took a step. A stage now stops only the pet's own walk;
a throw was never stopped and still is not.

